</picture>

    
    
</figure>

                                        
                                    
                                
                            
                        
                    
                
            
        </div><p><b><i>Figure 2. Tools that were used against our planted secrets, including the AI pentest agent (first row) and the Kali environment (aws-cli row).</i></b></p><p>The good news for defenders is that these tools tend to announce themselves – both Kali and ARTEX showed up in the user agent that AWS records in CloudTrail. The bad news is that this self-identification was only present in a small fraction of traffic.</p><p>
    <h2><a id="marketplace-resellers-stole-customer-prompts" href="#marketplace-resellers-stole-customer-prompts" name="marketplace-resellers-stole-customer-prompts" data-cms-ai="0">Marketplace resellers stole customer prompts</a></h2>


</p>

<p>The second finding didn’t require an exploit at all. The marketplace sellers that we caught only had to list a model at the lowest price, enable request logging, and wait. What stood out is how personal it was – these were individuals, working from what looked like home internet connections and personal computers, trying to break into our canary servers one login at a time.</p><p>In one case, we sent two prompts through a single seller’s offer. About a day and a half later, someone on a home broadband connection opened both secret URLs in a desktop browser and started guessing usernames at the login page. Prompts for the same model that went through a different seller were never touched, which tells us that the leak follows the seller and not the marketplace as a whole.</p><p>In another case, an attacker working from a Mac on a home broadband line in France took the passwords from two of our prompts and tried to log in as root over SSH, typing each attempt by hand. The same Mac later tested several of our AWS keys in a single session.</p><div data-align-center="">
            
            
                
                    
                        
                            
                                
                                    
                                        
                                            <figure>
    
