<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div data-hpc="true" containertiming="hpc"><article itemprop="text"><p dir="auto">
  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EL4CTEO/fast-anything/main/docs/assets/wordmark.png"><img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EL4CTEO/fast-anything/main/docs/assets/wordmark.png" alt="fast-anything" width="520"></a>
</p>
<p dir="auto"><b>Don't rewrite it in Rust. Rewrite the 5% that's slow.</b></p>
<p dir="auto">
  <a href="https://trendshift.io/repositories/371252" rel="nofollow"><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/6aaeefb75f495484e043c3f76cbbc3177a1675d9e1236e50ee84f25953971bf6/68747470733a2f2f7472656e6473686966742e696f2f6170692f62616467652f7265706f7369746f726965732f333731323532" alt="EL4CTEO/fast-anything | Trendshift" width="250" height="55" data-canonical-src="https://trendshift.io/api/badge/repositories/371252"></a>
</p>
<p dir="auto">
  <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@el4cteo/fast-anything" rel="nofollow"><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/72b66f7ee2b5c5ecf6417ab203aad85c80975231109c14ea723a4fda9d1e43a3/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f6e706d2f762f40656c346374656f2f666173742d616e797468696e673f636f6c6f723d663734633030266c6162656c3d6e706d" alt="npm" data-canonical-src="https://img.shields.io/npm/v/@el4cteo/fast-anything?color=f74c00&amp;label=npm"></a>
  <a href="https://crates.io/crates/fast-anything" rel="nofollow"><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/97ef44e04ab1a0dc3599ad7ef00aeab7f223a1eb597a0cb2919803ebc4770ffd/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f6372617465732f762f666173742d616e797468696e673f636f6c6f723d663734633030" alt="crates.io" data-canonical-src="https://img.shields.io/crates/v/fast-anything?color=f74c00"></a>
  <a href="https://github.com/EL4CTEO/fast-anything/actions/workflows/ci.yml"><img src="https://github.com/EL4CTEO/fast-anything/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg" alt="CI"></a>
  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://camo.githubusercontent."><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent." alt="Python, Node, TypeScript, Ruby, Java, Go, PHP, C, C++, C#" data-canonical-src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Python%20%C2%B7%20Node%20%C2%B7%20TypeScript%20%C2%B7%20Ruby%20%C2%B7%20Java%20%C2%B7%20Go%20%C2%B7%20PHP%20%C2%B7%20C%20%C2%B7%20C%2B%2B%20%C2%B7%20C%23-2563eb"></a>
  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/42e58082476adae2d034fbdd10a1e2350e5fa45460b10ba648ebe11a55d5780d/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f436c61756465253230436f64652d706c7567696e2d643937373537"><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/42e58082476adae2d034fbdd10a1e2350e5fa45460b10ba648ebe11a55d5780d/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f436c61756465253230436f64652d706c7567696e2d643937373537" alt="Claude Code plugin" data-canonical-src="https://img.shields.io/badge/Claude%20Code-plugin-d97757"></a>
  <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/f2a7efe759f76d6154a225388f54f878c5e6addab5d4fe8137c9fff8c2c962c8/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f4d43502d7365727665722d353535"><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/f2a7efe759f76d6154a225388f54f878c5e6addab5d4fe8137c9fff8c2c962c8/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f4d43502d7365727665722d353535" alt="MCP server" data-canonical-src="https://img.shields.io/badge/MCP-server-555"></a>
  <a href="https://github.com/EL4CTEO/fast-anything/blob/main/LICENSE"><img src="https://camo.githubusercontent.com/7fd6362a0f4a26782fad0bd5127f67d0cde2a7f29c359ee25e5452b95a636f49/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f6c6963656e73652d4d49542d353535" alt="MIT" data-canonical-src="https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-555"></a>
</p>
<p dir="auto">Rewriting a whole app in Rust costs months, minute-long compiles and gigabytes of <code>target/</code>. Most of the runtime sits in a few functions anyway.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>fast-anything</strong> finds those functions, has your coding agent port <em>only them</em> to Rust, proves the port gives the same results on real recorded calls, and swaps it in. One command, fully reversible.</p>
<p dir="auto"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EL4CTEO/fast-anything/main/docs/assets/demo.gif"><img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EL4CTEO/fast-anything/main/docs/assets/demo.gif" alt="fast-anything go --agent claude -- python app.py" width="820" data-animated-image=""></a></p>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Install</h2><a id="user-content-install" aria-label="Permalink: Install" href="#install"></a></p>
<div dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="npm i -g @el4cteo/fast-anything      # or: cargo install fast-anything"><pre>npm i -g @el4cteo/fast-anything      <span><span>#</span> or: cargo install fast-anything</span></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">Ports are compiled with your Rust toolchain (<a href="https://rustup.rs/" rel="nofollow">rustup</a>).</p>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Use</h2><a id="user-content-use" aria-label="Permalink: Use" href="#use"></a></p>
<div dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="fast-anything go --agent claude -- python app.py     # or: -- node app.ts / bun app.ts / deno run -A app.ts / ruby app.rb / java App.java / mvn exec:java / gradle run / go run . / php app.php / clang -O2 main.c"><pre>fast-anything go --agent claude -- python app.py     <span><span>#</span> or: -- node app.ts / bun app.ts / deno run -A app.ts / ruby app.rb / java App.java / mvn exec:java / gradle run / go run . / php app.php / clang -O2 main.c</span></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">Or step by step:</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>command</th>
<th>what it does</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>scan -- &lt;cmd&gt;</code></td>
<td>profiles the app, ranks functions by time × how portable they are</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>port [id]</code></td>
<td>records up to 500 real calls, creates a one-function Rust crate + <code>TASK.md</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>verify</code></td>
<td>release-builds the port and replays every recorded call</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>enable</code> / <code>disable</code></td>
<td>swaps the Rust in or out (one marked block, removed byte for byte)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>bench</code></td>
<td>times the whole app, original vs Rust, interleaved runs</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>report</code></td>
<td>markdown + SVG card for your PR</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>doctor</code></td>
<td>checks Rust, your runtimes and your agents</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir="auto"><code>--agent</code> takes <code>claude</code>, <code>codex</code>, or any command that reads a prompt on stdin. Without it, hand <code>TASK.md</code> to whatever you use.</p>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Proof, not vibes</h2><a id="user-content-proof-not-vibes" aria-label="Permalink: Proof, not vibes" href="#proof-not-vibes"></a></p>
<p dir="auto"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EL4CTEO/fast-anything/main/docs/assets/verify.gif"><img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EL4CTEO/fast-anything/main/docs/assets/verify.gif" alt="verify catches a wrong port" width="820" data-animated-image=""></a></p>
<p dir="auto">That port looked right but compared bytes instead of characters. 148 of 500 real calls caught it. On top of the recorded calls, fast-anything derives extra cases and lets the original answer them: edge cases (NaN, ±infinity, -0.0, zero and ±1, non-ASCII text, empty and up to 16× bigger inputs) and shrunk inputs (tiny and random slices). Nothing is enabled until every case matches: same values (floats within 1e-9), errors where the original errors. A port that is right but slower per call than the original (calling into Rust costs more than the work saved) isn't enabled either. <code>FAST_ANYTHING_DISABLE=1</code> runs the original any time.</p>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Results</h2><a id="user-content-results" aria-label="Permalink: Results" href="#results"></a></p>
<p dir="auto">Real runs on an i5-10500, Windows 11 (C and C++: a 4-core GitHub Actions Linux runner). Reproduce them from <a href="https://github.com/EL4CTEO/fast-anything/blob/main/examples"><code>examples/</code></a>.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>app</th>
