<p dir="auto">fast-anything ports the outermost loop it can, not the tiny function called inside it, so the app crosses into Rust once instead of millions of times. Porting only the inner <code>levenshtein</code> gave 35× and 1.9×.</p>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Why not rewrite it all?</h2><a id="user-content-why-not-rewrite-it-all" aria-label="Permalink: Why not rewrite it all?" href="#why-not-rewrite-it-all"></a></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><strong>Compile time</strong>: each port is a one-function crate. Seconds, not minutes.</li>
<li><strong>Cache</strong>: every port shares one <code>.fast/target</code>. Delete it whenever you like.</li>
<li><strong>Risk</strong>: your code stays as it is. Rust is opt-in per function, checked against real behavior.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Agents</h2><a id="user-content-agents" aria-label="Permalink: Agents" href="#agents"></a></p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><strong>Claude Code plugin</strong>: <code>/plugin marketplace add EL4CTEO/fast-anything</code>, then <code>/plugin install fast-anything@fast-anything</code> and <code>/fast-anything:fast python app.py</code></li>
<li><strong>MCP server</strong> (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor…), built into the binary: <code>claude mcp add fast-anything -- fast-anything mcp</code>. 8 tools: <code>fast_scan</code>, <code>fast_port</code>, <code>fast_verify</code>, <code>fast_enable</code>, <code>fast_disable</code>, <code>fast_bench</code>, <code>fast_report</code>, <code>fast_status</code>.</li>
<li><strong>Skill</strong>: <a href="https://github.com/EL4CTEO/fast-anything/blob/main/skills/fast-anything/SKILL.md"><code>skills/fast-anything</code></a> teaches any agent the loop.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Languages</h2><a id="user-content-languages" aria-label="Permalink: Languages" href="#languages"></a></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>language</th>
<th>binding</th>
<th>status</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Python 3.10+</td>
<td>PyO3</td>
<td>✅</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>JavaScript / TypeScript (Node 22+, Bun, Deno 2+: <code>bun app.ts</code>, <code>deno run -A app.ts</code>)</td>
